\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Monte Carlo trial generation and evaluation pipeline. Each of 20~nominal snapshots yields 200~perturbed trials; each trial is evaluated by both the conventional and \textsc {sambp}{} Stage-2 decision paths.}}{4}{figure.caption.4}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Aggregate performance comparison. Conventional (blue) vs.\ \textsc {sambp}{} Stage-2 (red). Both methods share identical FPR and specificity; the \textsc {sambp}{} sensitivity shortfall is concentrated in three-phase bus differential scenarios.}}{5}{figure.caption.10}%
